From 7614eedf793109b668ae26cdcca71a4128189d67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio D'Achille <existenz70@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:27:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Seamless tile: LocalImageGenerator reads seamlessTile
 for the four families; whole decode, no tiled diffusion

- LocalImageGenerator.generate reads GenerationConfiguration.seamlessTile only for Krea 2, Z-Image,
  FLUX.2 and FLUX.3 and runs on a copy that carries it, with tiled diffusion and tiled decoding off;
  a size that is not a multiple of 16 px is refused with an error.
- Every sampler gets `seamless` (Sampler protocol) and passes it to its UNetFixedEncoder, base and
  refiner; the RoPE is built per pass, so a HiRes fix pass uses its own grid.
- FirstStage.wrap: the Z-Image, FLUX.2/3 and Krea 2 decoders are built NHWC with the wrap, at the
  whole latent size (no tiles, no forced Wan tiling, no cached decoder); ModelPreloader keys its
  cached decoder on the wrap.
- JSGenerationConfiguration.seamlessTile (absent when 0) so draw-things-cli --config-json reaches it.
- Krea 2 min_turns 0.5 -> 1.0: at 0.5 the DT Krea 2 turbo repeated the tile twice inside the tile
  (stone texture, autocorrelation 0.90 at half the tile; 0.19 at 1.0, no fault lines on planks).
- Apps/SeamlessTileTest/e2e.sh (generate + ComfyUI seam_check) and baseline.sha256 (bcdc18f, flag off):
  all four families PASS both directions; flag-off output byte-identical; Ming ignores the flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
